From: amatiramisu <261696294+amatiramisu@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 05:59:25 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] winewayland.drv: Ask for fullscreen again while a
 configure waits.

A DSR mode change can leave a borderless window maximized with a
configure that is never acknowledged, so the game stays black. Request
fullscreen again in that case.
---
 dlls/winewayland.drv/window.c | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/winewayland.drv/window.c b/dlls/winewayland.drv/window.c
index bbff6be2c7d..c263015c5cb 100644
--- a/dlls/winewayland.drv/window.c
+++ b/dlls/winewayland.drv/window.c
@@ -1071,6 +1071,23 @@ static void wayland_surface_update_state_toplevel(struct wayland_surface *surfac
     /* set_minimized is a one-shot request. */
     if (!window->minimized) surface->comitted.minimized = FALSE;
 
+    /* A configure the window has already taken stays authoritative only while
+     * the window agrees with it. A maximized window that covers its monitor
+     * after the compositor's resize (a desktop mode change left it briefly
+     * smaller) is fullscreen for Win32, so that configure can never be
+     * acknowledged and the surface stops presenting. Ask for fullscreen. */
+    if (processing_config && surface->processing.processed &&
+        (window->state & WAYLAND_SURFACE_CONFIG_STATE_FULLSCREEN) &&
+        !(surface->processing.state & WAYLAND_SURFACE_CONFIG_STATE_FULLSCREEN))
+    {
+        TRACE("hwnd=%p fullscreen again during configure state=%#x\n",
+              surface->hwnd, surface->processing.state);
+        if ((surface->processing.state & WAYLAND_SURFACE_CONFIG_STATE_MAXIMIZED) &&
+            !surface->fullscreen_requested)
+            xdg_toplevel_unset_maximized(surface->xdg_toplevel);
+        processing_config = FALSE;
+    }
+
     /* If we are not processing a compositor configure, use the latest Win32
      * window state to update the Wayland state. */
     if (!processing_config)
